  "description": "Use potere and volere to ask for help and talk about travel plans.",
  "grammar_note": "Potere means “can / to be able to” (posso = I can, puoi = you can). Volere means “to want” (voglio = I want, vuoi = you want). These verbs are followed by an infinitive: Posso andare? = Can I go?",
